From 9a599ae63ff12b1b0963f71e46375c5713ff4456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Zhang <zxh@xh-zhang.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mm: xswap: test an eight-chunk cap on metadata growth

Reference pilots executed 12 to 16 growth operations. Raising the cap
can satisfy a large occupancy deficit with fewer mapping episodes.
It does not force an eight-chunk allocation when less is needed.

Keep the occupancy target, device maximum clamp, stale-range checks,
allocation rollback, no-reclaim scope and publication ordering intact.
The experiment may allocate larger bursts or retain more metadata.
No throughput or latency improvement is assumed from fewer calls.

This independent candidate follows a smaller-shrink-minimum experiment
whose mixed retention results did not justify promotion.
---
 mm/swapfile.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/swapfile.c b/mm/swapfile.c
index 180cf538f..70c075cd2 100644
--- a/mm/swapfile.c
+++ b/mm/swapfile.c
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
 #define XSWAP_SHRINK_UNTIL	70
 #define XSWAP_GROW_UNTIL	65
 #define XSWAP_GROW_WHEN		85
-#define XSWAP_GROW_CHUNKS	4
+#define XSWAP_GROW_CHUNKS	8
 
 static bool xswap_should_grow(struct swap_info_struct *si);
 static unsigned long xswap_grow(struct swap_info_struct *si);
